WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.070 line:80%
A robot has to find a pallet
and line up with its fork openings.

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:08.620 line:80%
That is a perception problem
before it is a control problem.

00:00:09.844 --> 00:00:14.374 line:80%
Python drives Blender
to vary the scene, lighting and camera.

00:00:14.384 --> 00:00:19.644 line:80%
Each synthetic image comes with its
bounding boxes and keypoint annotations.

00:00:20.935 --> 00:00:25.085 line:80%
Detectors were trained
and evaluated on real images:

00:00:25.095 --> 00:00:31.246 line:80%
synthetic pre-training held detection and
pose quality from a small annotated set,

00:00:31.256 --> 00:00:33.496 line:80%
where real-only training lagged.

00:00:34.804 --> 00:00:38.864 line:80%
Keypoints give the approach
a geometry a box cannot.

00:00:38.874 --> 00:00:43.774 line:80%
Synthetic pre-training reduced lateral
misalignment at the target point.

00:00:44.824 --> 00:00:50.114 line:80%
A FastAPI and WebSocket service
connects the detector to simulation

00:00:50.374 --> 00:00:53.134 line:80%
and the existing navigation stack.

00:00:53.144 --> 00:00:56.264 line:80%
The same model path leads
to edge deployment.

00:00:57.047 --> 00:01:01.797 line:80%
Closed-loop tests run the approach
in the partner’s PyBullet simulator:

00:01:01.807 --> 00:01:05.807 line:80%
camera input in, perception output back
to the controller.

00:01:07.057 --> 00:01:10.427 line:80%
The simulator and dashboard were built
by the partner.

00:01:10.437 --> 00:01:15.387 line:80%
The detector, its service and their
integration are what this film shows.

00:01:16.511 --> 00:01:20.851 line:80%
Synthetic scenes, a trained detector
and an onboard Jetson:

00:01:20.861 --> 00:01:23.691 line:80%
one perception path
from data to the robot.
